  expect(await save({ cli: OTHER() })).toMatchObject({ saved: true, restarting: true })
  await vi.waitFor(() => expect(restarts).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1))
  // Other fields of the Source take effect without a restart.
  expect(await save({ pollSeconds: 120 })).toMatchObject({ saved: true, restarting: false })
  expect(restarts).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)
  expect((await runtime.settings.save('executor', { ...runtime.store.settings().executor, prepare: 'true' }, runtime.store.blockRevision('executor'), 'panel')).restarting).toBe(false)
  // A save of another block during the account check is kept: the check runs first, then the save merges.
  const pending = save({ cli: AGENT() })
  await runtime.settings.save('policy', { ...runtime.store.settings().policy, rules: [] }, runtime.store.blockRevision('policy'), 'panel')
  await pending
  expect(runtime.store.settings().policy.rules).toEqual([])
  expect(runtime.store.settings().sources.github!.config).toMatchObject({ cli: AGENT() })
  const feishuSave = (cli: string) => runtime.settings.save('source:feishu', { enabled: true, config: { ...runtime.store.settings().sources.feishu!.config, cli } },
    runtime.store.blockRevision('source:feishu'), 'panel')
upstream/superagent/docs/004-prompts.md:59:The environment section gives the main Session deployment-wide values and each Executor its Ticket-specific values. The Policy section is regenerated from settings on every model request. It contains the Policy version, accept mode, the explicit-request exemption, and enabled rules as `- <name> (<id>): <instruction>`, or a statement that none is enabled. It is last so a Policy change leaves the preceding prompt text unchanged.
upstream/superagent/docs/004-prompts.md:84:- **Ask through `human_action`.** The Executor puts one concrete question in its Report, and the main Session forwards it unchanged. If a person's message prompted the question, it names that message and the host asks there. Otherwise it asks in the Ticket's original conversation. Already authorized work can continue meanwhile.
upstream/superagent/docs/004-prompts.md:86:- **A person's pause holds** across follow-ups, new Executor Sessions and restarts until a person lifts it. Automatic feedback never resumes paused work.
upstream/superagent/docs/004-prompts.md:95:- Sessions read the latest version on every model request, including later steps in the same turn. Saving does not restart, cancel or wake a Session. The host records the revisions each Session used; an Executor can read any revision it worked under.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:7:- **A dedicated DeepSeek Harness profile**, called `superagent` in this guide. Create it from the Web profile template. It loads the bundle and serves its panel on `127.0.0.1`. Keep it separate from the profile you work in: the plugin changes process-wide `PATH` and git settings, and its process needs independent restarts and upgrades.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:98:After the first start, edit machine limits in **Settings → Deployment** or the DeepSeek Harness Plugin Manager. Changes apply without restart. `stateDir` cannot be changed there. Invalid values or unknown configuration keys prevent startup; the log identifies the key.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:109:`stop` and `restart` request graceful shutdown and wait up to five minutes for Executors. They never force-kill the process or touch other tmux sessions.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:113:`status`, `start` and `restart` exit with one of four codes:
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:118:| 1 | It does not run, runs twice, does not answer, or its runtime reports an error; a restart may fix it |
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:119:| 2 | It runs, but a part other than the runtime, such as a Source or a Policy sync (`sync:<source id>`), reports an error; a restart does not fix it |
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:120:| 3 | It runs and waits for setup; a restart does not fix it |
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:124:`status` returns failed parts and their details under `errors`, and setup requirements under `setup`. `start` and `restart` print those problems as lines; they exit 1 if the service never comes up. Only an intentional `stop` pauses automatic recovery.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:138:Check dsh-superagent: run `scripts/dsh-superagent --profile superagent status` in <checkout>. Exit 0: do nothing and say nothing. Exit 2: do not restart; tell me each part under `errors` with its detail, unless you already told me about the same ones. Exit 3: do not restart; tell me what `setup` says setup needs, unless you already told me. If it reports manually_stopped: true, leave it stopped. Otherwise (exit 1) run `scripts/dsh-superagent --profile superagent --respect-stop restart`, which exits the same way: 0 means it recovered, so say nothing; 2 and 3 are reported as above; if it exits 1 or fails otherwise, read the newest .artifacts/dsh-superagent-superagent-*.log and the Troubleshooting section of docs/006-deployment.md, fix what you can, and tell me what was wrong and what you did.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:141:`--respect-stop` preserves an intentional stop. Only `stop` writes the marker; `start` clears it. `restart` writes no marker, so the check can recover a restart whose shutdown timed out.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:174:| `PUT settings/<block>` with `{"value": …, "revision": n}` | Saves one block: `saved`, the block's new `revision`, `policy_changed` and `restarting`. `value` is the whole block, as `GET settings` holds it; a missing key takes its default |
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:176:| `POST setup/check` | Runs setup again by restarting dsh-superagent: `restarting: true`. Refused when setup has nothing to fix |
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:207:Changing a repository or CLI runs the corresponding setup check first. A failed check returns 400 with details in `setup`. A successful account change, or any save while setup is pending, returns `restarting: true`. The API is temporarily unavailable while the application restarts.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:238:4. Run `scripts/dsh-superagent restart` and inspect its status.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:240:A restart ends running Assignments and starts replacements with recovery notes. Team text and overridden prompt parts are retained; parts without overrides follow the new defaults. Review parts marked **Default updated** after upgrading.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:242:A database migrated by a newer version cannot be opened by an older one. Rollback therefore requires the pre-upgrade backup. After upgrading DeepSeek Harness itself, restart the running instance so the panel loads matching artifacts.
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:266:| `status` exits 2 | A part reports an error, which a restart does not fix: `errors` names each part, as listed under Management API, with its detail; each part clears its own entry once it works again |
upstream/superagent/docs/006-deployment.md:270:| The panel says dsh-superagent is not answering | It is restarting, or did not start because of its configuration; the DeepSeek Harness log names the cause |
import { execFile, spawn } from 'node:child_process'
import { chmodSync, mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, rmSync, symlinkSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os'
import { join } from 'node:path'
import { promisify } from 'node:util'
import { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest'
import { SENSITIVE_ENV_PATTERN, type SubprocessRuntime } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess'
import { GIT_LOCATION, agentVariables, credentialHelper, runAsWorker, verifyDirectory, withoutDirectory, workerBin, workerGitConfig, writeEnvironment }
  from '../src/infra/environment.ts'
import { CliError } from '../src/infra/commands.ts'
import { MeshAccessDenied } from '../src/extensions/mesh/auth.ts'
import { testDeployment } from './fixtures/deployment.ts'
import { gitEnv } from './fixtures/git.ts'

// Git and shell subprocesses can exceed the 5s default timeout when the test suite runs in parallel.
vi.setConfig({ testTimeout: 30_000 })
const exec = promisify(execFile)
it('refuses to publish a shim when authority is revoked after its temporary file was written', async () => {
  const deployment = testDeployment({ stateDir: dir })
  await writeEnvironment(deployment, [])
  const before = readFileSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'gh'), 'utf8')
  let revoked = false
  const authorize = () => {
    if (readdirSync(workerBin(dir)).some(name => name.startsWith('.gh.') && name.endsWith('.tmp'))) revoked = true
    if (revoked) throw new MeshAccessDenied()
  }
  await expect(writeEnvironment({ ...deployment, github: { ...deployment.github, cli: '/fixture/changed-gh' } }, [], authorize)).rejects.toThrow(MeshAccessDenied)
  expect(revoked).toBe(true)
  expect(readFileSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'gh'), 'utf8')).toBe(before)
  expect(readdirSync(workerBin(dir)).some(name => name.endsWith('.tmp'))).toBe(false)
})
let dir: string
const program = (path: string, body: string): string => { writeFileSync(path, `#!/bin/sh\n${body}\n`); chmodSync(path, 0o755); return path }
/** Worker shell environment after DSH strips credential-shaped variables. */
const workerEnv = (env: Record<string, string | undefined>): Record<string, string> =>
  Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(env).filter((entry): entry is [string, string] => entry[1] !== undefined && !SENSITIVE_ENV_PATTERN.test(entry[0])))
beforeEach(() => { dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'environment-')); mkdirSync(join(dir, 'real')) })
afterEach(() => { rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }) })

describe('worker shims', () => {
  it('run a wrapper that calls `gh` by name without reaching the shim again, and keep the caller\'s other PATH entries', async () => {
    program(join(dir, 'real', 'gh'), 'echo "{\\"login\\":\\"agent-bot\\",\\"config\\":\\"$GH_CONFIG_DIR\\",\\"path\\":\\"$PATH\\"}"')
    const wrapper = program(join(dir, 'gh-agent'), `GH_CONFIG_DIR=${dir}/agent-config exec gh "$@"`)
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir, github: { ...testDeployment().github, cli: wrapper }, feishu: undefined }), [])
    const bin = workerBin(dir)
    const path = [bin, join(dir, 'venv'), join(dir, 'real'), '/usr/bin', '/bin'].join(':')
    const { stdout } = await exec('gh', ['api', 'user'], { env: { PATH: path }, timeout: 10_000 })
    expect(JSON.parse(stdout)).toEqual({ login: 'agent-bot', config: `${dir}/agent-config`, path: [join(dir, 'venv'), join(dir, 'real'), '/usr/bin', '/bin'].join(':') })
  })
  it('make `lark-cli` fail without a Feishu bot and each blocked command fail with the agent\'s login', async () => {
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir, feishu: undefined }), ['personal-gh'])
    const bin = workerBin(dir)
    await expect(exec(join(bin, 'lark-cli'), ['im', '+chat-list'])).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: 1, stderr: 'lark-cli is unavailable: this installation has no Feishu bot.\n' })
    await expect(exec(join(bin, 'personal-gh'), [])).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: 1, stderr: 'personal-gh is blocked in this installation; use gh, which acts as agent-bot.\n' })
  })
  it('keep `gh` and `lark-cli` working, and shim no `git`, when the blocked commands name the commands workers need', async () => {
    const gh = program(join(dir, 'gh-agent'), 'echo gh "$@"'), lark = program(join(dir, 'lark-bot'), 'echo lark "$@"')
    const base = testDeployment()
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir, github: { ...base.github, cli: gh }, feishu: { ...base.feishu!, cli: lark } }), ['gh', 'git', 'lark-cli'])
    const bin = workerBin(dir)
    expect([(await exec(join(bin, 'gh'), ['api', 'user'])).stdout, (await exec(join(bin, 'lark-cli'), ['im'])).stdout]).toEqual(['gh api user\n', 'lark im\n'])
    expect(readdirSync(bin)).not.toContain('git')
  })
  it('replace only what dsh-superagent wrote and refuse anything else in its places', async () => {
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), ['old-cli'])
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), [])
    expect(readdirSync(workerBin(dir)).sort()).toEqual(['gh', 'lark-cli'])
    // A file that merely contains the marker on a later line, a symlink to a shim, and a foreign gitconfig are all rejected.
    writeFileSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'notes'), `notes\nmore\n${readFileSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'gh'), 'utf8').split('\n')[1]}\n`)
    await expect(writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), [])).rejects.toThrow(`${join(workerBin(dir), 'notes')} was not written by dsh-superagent`)
    rmSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'notes'))
    symlinkSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'gh'), join(workerBin(dir), 'link'))
    await expect(writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), [])).rejects.toThrow('link was not written by dsh-superagent')
    rmSync(join(workerBin(dir), 'link'))
    writeFileSync(workerGitConfig(dir), '[user]\n\tname = someone\n')
    await expect(writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), [])).rejects.toThrow(`${workerGitConfig(dir)} was not written by dsh-superagent`)
    expect(readFileSync(workerGitConfig(dir), 'utf8')).toBe('[user]\n\tname = someone\n')
  })
  it('replaces the files it wrote under the project\'s earlier names', async () => {
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), ['old-cli', 'older-cli'])
    const legacy = (file: string, name: string) => writeFileSync(file, readFileSync(file, 'utf8').replace('Written by dsh-superagent', `Written by ${name}`))
    legacy(join(workerBin(dir), 'old-cli'), 'dsh-tag'); legacy(join(workerBin(dir), 'older-cli'), 'dsh-freelancer'); legacy(workerGitConfig(dir), 'dsh-go')
    await writeEnvironment(testDeployment({ stateDir: dir }), [])
    expect(readdirSync(workerBin(dir)).sort()).toEqual(['gh', 'lark-cli'])
    expect(readFileSync(workerGitConfig(dir), 'utf8')).toContain('Written by dsh-superagent')
  })
})

describe('agent git configuration', () => {
  it('ignores the operator\'s global and system git configuration, also after DSH drops credential-shaped variables', async () => {
    const home = join(dir, 'home'); mkdirSync(home)
    // Operator configuration that rewrites HTTPS to SSH, enables commit signing, and sets a credential helper.
    writeFileSync(join(home, '.gitconfig'), '[url "git@github.com:"]\n\tinsteadOf = https://github.com/\n[commit]\n\tgpgsign = true\n[credential]\n\thelper = osxkeychain\n')
    const deployment = testDeployment({ stateDir: dir, github: { ...testDeployment().github, cli: '/opt/agent tools/gh' } })
    await writeEnvironment(deployment, [])
    // Operator identity variables and git's fallback from the OS username must not apply to worker commits.
    const env = workerEnv({ PATH: process.env.PATH, HOME: home, GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1', GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: 'core.abbrev', GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: '12', GIT_AUTHOR_NAME: 'Operator', GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL: 'operator@example.com', ...agentVariables(dir) })
    const git = async (...args: string[]): Promise<string> => (await exec('git', args, { cwd: dir, env })).stdout.trim()
    await git('init', '-q', 'repo')
    await exec('git', ['-C', 'repo', 'remote', 'add', 'origin', 'git@github.com:acme/widgets.git'], { cwd: dir, env })
    expect(await git('-C', 'repo', 'remote', 'get-url', '--push', 'origin')).toBe('https://github.com/acme/widgets.git')
    expect(await git('config', '--show-origin', '--get-all', 'credential.https://github.com.helper')).toBe(`file:${workerGitConfig(dir)}\t${credentialHelper('/opt/agent tools/gh')}`)
    expect(await git('config', '--get-all', 'credential.helper')).toBe('')
    await expect(git('config', 'commit.gpgsign')).rejects.toThrow()
    await expect(git('config', 'core.abbrev')).rejects.toThrow()
    expect(env).not.toHaveProperty('GIT_AUTHOR_NAME')
    expect(env).not.toHaveProperty('GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL')
    await expect(git('-C', 'repo', 'commit', '--allow-empty', '-q', '-m', 'without identity')).rejects.toMatchObject({ stderr: expect.stringContaining('no email was given') })
    await git('-C', 'repo', '-c', 'user.name=Alice', '-c', 'user.email=alice@example.com', 'commit', '--allow-empty', '-q', '-m', 'with identity')
    expect(await git('-C', 'repo', 'log', '-1', '--format=%an <%ae> / %cn <%ce>')).toBe('Alice <alice@example.com> / Alice <alice@example.com>')
  })
})

